1
00:00:38,664 --> 00:00:41,959
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

2
00:00:42,501 --> 00:00:45,295
- Are they here?
- Yes.

3
00:01:27,963 --> 00:01:30,674
Meet HAN's CEO, Ms. Han Jeong-yeon.

4
00:01:33,969 --> 00:01:35,012
It's a pleasure.

5
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:37,472
Welcome to Appello.

6
00:01:52,404 --> 00:01:55,407
Nice to meet you, Mr. Kang Ha-gi.

7
00:02:17,471 --> 00:02:19,264
Thank you for coming here in person.

8
00:02:19,765 --> 00:02:22,183
It must've been a long trip.

9
00:02:22,184 --> 00:02:24,353
Let's go inside.
Allow me to escort you.

10
00:02:27,064 --> 00:02:28,899
This way, please.

11
00:02:29,691 --> 00:02:31,234
Watch out for the steps.

12
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:33,779
- Please.
- I'm fine.

13
00:02:38,450 --> 00:02:40,702
- Good luck.
- Thank you.

14
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:46,333
She's gorgeous.

15
00:02:52,631 --> 00:02:56,051
The proposal I received from Appello
was impressive.

16
00:02:57,469 --> 00:02:59,179
So I wanted to come here myself.

17
00:03:05,477 --> 00:03:06,561
HAN has selected

18
00:03:07,479 --> 00:03:10,982
SE:ON and Appello
as our preferred bidders

19
00:03:11,233 --> 00:03:12,943
and would like to give you
the same assignment.

20
00:03:14,945 --> 00:03:15,946
Sorry?

21
00:03:16,947 --> 00:03:17,948
It's simple.

22
00:03:18,490 --> 00:03:20,951
Who are HAN's customers?

23
00:03:21,827 --> 00:03:22,953
Let's define that.

24
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:27,916
Are you asking us
to conduct customer profiling?

25
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:29,375
You're right.

26
00:03:29,376 --> 00:03:32,713
We'll select our partner based
on the pitches from both companies.

27
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:34,673
Goodness.

28
00:03:38,176 --> 00:03:39,761
This won't be easy.

29
00:03:42,597 --> 00:03:43,598
It's tricky.

30
00:03:48,895 --> 00:03:50,564
EPISODE 10

31
00:03:53,483 --> 00:03:54,526
How am I supposed

32
00:03:55,986 --> 00:03:57,070
to make sense of this situation?

33
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:01,616
I recently ran into her by chance.

34
00:04:02,284 --> 00:04:04,745
She wanted a tour of Appello,
so I welcomed her

35
00:04:05,036 --> 00:04:06,455
and she stabs my back like this.

36
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:09,249
It's just business.

37
00:04:12,127 --> 00:04:15,046
Chan only found out today
that I was HAN's CEO.

38
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:20,302
Anyway.

39
00:04:21,094 --> 00:04:22,721
It's great to get together again.

40
00:04:23,513 --> 00:04:24,639
The three of us.

41
00:04:30,437 --> 00:04:32,481
Then the CEOs should chat.

42
00:04:32,814 --> 00:04:34,191
I have to be somewhere.

43
00:04:50,290 --> 00:04:53,293
I can't believe the CEO came
instead of sending the managers.

44
00:04:54,002 --> 00:04:56,170
That's cool.

45
00:04:56,171 --> 00:04:59,424
Didn't something seem kind of odd?

46
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:01,092
What? How?

47
00:05:02,010 --> 00:05:04,429
- It was Mr. Kang's face.
- Yes?

48
00:05:04,805 --> 00:05:07,015
It seemed like they were

49
00:05:08,225 --> 00:05:09,392
acquainted.

50
00:05:15,232 --> 00:05:18,192
Who's the director in charge
of this store?

51
00:05:18,193 --> 00:05:20,403
Nice to meet you, Mr. Kang Ha-gi.

52
00:05:36,294 --> 00:05:37,337
Who is this?

53
00:05:38,421 --> 00:05:40,549
She's the woman from the photo.

54
00:05:42,884 --> 00:05:44,386
You haven't changed

55
00:05:45,262 --> 00:05:46,429
both in your departure...

56
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:53,520
and return.

57
00:05:56,648 --> 00:05:57,774
Let's eat dinner.

58
00:06:00,193 --> 00:06:01,319
I've got plans.

59
00:06:03,905 --> 00:06:05,740
I'm asking as HAN's CEO.

60
00:06:14,249 --> 00:06:15,792
I have something important to say.

61
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:27,053
I'm sorry, Da-reum.

62
00:06:27,345 --> 00:06:30,140
My meeting with Ms. Han
is taking longer than I thought.

63
00:06:30,974 --> 00:06:31,975
I'm sorry.

64
00:06:33,560 --> 00:06:34,561
CEO KANG HA-GI OF APPELLO

65
00:06:36,187 --> 00:06:37,271
It's all right.

66
00:06:37,272 --> 00:06:39,816
It's important for our company,
so it should be your priority.

67
00:06:40,233 --> 00:06:41,318
I understand.

68
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:47,407
What is this?

69
00:06:47,782 --> 00:06:51,036
I was excited to meet
Namda's first-ever boyfriend.

70
00:06:51,620 --> 00:06:53,288
It's a bit much
to bail on us at the last minute.

71
00:06:53,914 --> 00:06:56,207
This meeting is really important.

72
00:06:56,458 --> 00:06:58,001
Please let him off.

73
00:06:58,752 --> 00:07:00,795
- Wait, Ha-gi isn't coming today?
- My gosh.

74
00:07:01,421 --> 00:07:02,464
Hello.

75
00:07:02,839 --> 00:07:04,423
What's going on?

76
00:07:04,424 --> 00:07:06,842
I wanted to sneak in
and introduce myself too.

77
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:07,928
Why would you do that?

78
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:09,763
You're Da-reum's friend.

79
00:07:10,096 --> 00:07:11,388
I'm Ha-gi's friend.

80
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:13,515
Da-reum and Ha-gi are a couple.

81
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:14,809
Mi-mi and I are practically...

82
00:07:15,185 --> 00:07:17,312
Instructor and student, right?

83
00:07:19,064 --> 00:07:22,275
Well, allow me to treat you
in Ha-gi's place today.

84
00:07:22,734 --> 00:07:24,152
- What would you like?
- What?

85
00:07:24,611 --> 00:07:25,946
Let's order. What do you want?

86
00:07:26,279 --> 00:07:27,696
- I'm okay.
- Excuse me!

87
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:28,698
My gosh.

88
00:07:29,157 --> 00:07:30,449
What should we order?

89
00:07:30,450 --> 00:07:32,327
- Can we order a lot?
- Yes, as much as you want.

90
00:07:34,955 --> 00:07:38,083
I thought you'd be glad to see me.

91
00:07:40,919 --> 00:07:42,671
You aren't exactly a fond memory,
so not really.

92
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,218
I found out much later.

93
00:07:49,094 --> 00:07:52,138
MAKER SPACE WORKSHOP

94
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:06,194
- No, not really for me.
- Really?

95
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:14,577
- Then do you have to do it?
- Maybe later.

96
00:08:37,892 --> 00:08:39,019
Chan!

97
00:08:46,609 --> 00:08:48,945
The reason
Chan became a trainee and left

98
00:08:50,071 --> 00:08:51,322
was because of us.

99
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:54,617
That day

100
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:57,287
I had lost my closest friend.

101
00:09:00,957 --> 00:09:02,751
Of course, he's back in my life.

102
00:09:05,837 --> 00:09:07,088
But we still don't talk about that.

103
00:09:10,508 --> 00:09:12,760
Then you left to study abroad
without a word

104
00:09:12,761 --> 00:09:13,887
so I was left alone.

105
00:09:16,014 --> 00:09:17,515
How is that a great memory?

106
00:09:20,018 --> 00:09:21,102
You're right.

107
00:09:22,604 --> 00:09:24,689
I should've told you before I left.

108
00:09:27,108 --> 00:09:28,318
Was it tough for you?

109
00:09:33,698 --> 00:09:35,533
We weren't that serious.

110
00:09:38,078 --> 00:09:39,287
We only dated for a few months.

111
00:09:44,626 --> 00:09:45,710
From time to time

112
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:48,004
whenever I thought of Korea

113
00:09:49,881 --> 00:09:51,216
I thought of you.

114
00:09:54,677 --> 00:09:56,846
What's this important thing
you wanted to tell me as HAN's CEO?

115
00:10:05,146 --> 00:10:06,856
Wait, who?

116
00:10:07,482 --> 00:10:08,525
Han Jeong-yeon?

117
00:10:08,942 --> 00:10:10,151
From school?

118
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:13,695
Oh, so they weren't classmates,
but she was a senior.

119
00:10:13,696 --> 00:10:15,490
Yes, a year older.

120
00:10:16,324 --> 00:10:17,742
This is getting interesting.

121
00:10:18,284 --> 00:10:21,454
I mean, she's Ha-gi's first love.

122
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:24,456
Back then, she was
so popular with the guys.

123
00:10:24,457 --> 00:10:27,377
Gosh, don't even get me started.
Chan was into her too.

124
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:31,881
She was pretty much
everyone's first love.

125
00:10:32,173 --> 00:10:34,801
Gosh, this is fascinating.

126
00:10:35,051 --> 00:10:36,761
How did they reunite?

127
00:10:42,851 --> 00:10:46,729
- So she was his first love?
- Yes.

128
00:10:47,814 --> 00:10:50,984
It was back in high school.
That's an ancient story.

129
00:10:51,943 --> 00:10:53,111
She's still gorgeous, right?

130
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:58,158
My heart would race so quickly
if I ran into my first love.

131
00:11:02,996 --> 00:11:04,872
- Let's just drink, shall we?
- Yes, cheers.

132
00:11:04,873 --> 00:11:07,876
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

133
00:11:18,469 --> 00:11:19,928
HAN DIDN'T CREATE A BRAND
BUT AN AESTHETIC

134
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:21,054
SE:ON'S DEFINITION
OF HAN'S PHILOSOPHY

135
00:11:21,055 --> 00:11:22,432
SE:ON and Appello's proposals

136
00:11:22,891 --> 00:11:24,767
looked far too similar.

137
00:11:25,977 --> 00:11:28,563
It's not a coincidence, is it?

138
00:11:32,817 --> 00:11:34,319
There's a spy among us.

139
00:11:35,737 --> 00:11:38,406
- I've been looking.
- I knew it.

140
00:11:39,991 --> 00:11:41,784
Does anyone come to mind?

141
00:11:43,411 --> 00:11:44,412
I'm not...

142
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:47,582
completely sure yet.

143
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:53,087
I thought you and I

144
00:11:54,339 --> 00:11:56,716
might share the same goal.

145
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:01,763
I didn't meet with SE:ON
to sign with them.

146
00:12:03,014 --> 00:12:04,140
I went to get revenge.

147
00:12:16,736 --> 00:12:19,322
I'll get my revenge,
and you can find the spy.

148
00:12:20,615 --> 00:12:22,951
Don't you think we could pull it off
if we worked together?

149
00:12:24,619 --> 00:12:25,745
Think about it.

150
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:33,753
Jeez.

151
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:39,591
Hey, you're his current girlfriend.

152
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:41,969
And you're absolutely charming too.

153
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:45,472
Who cares about first love?
Darn it. She has nothing on you.

154
00:12:45,473 --> 00:12:47,766
- She doesn't!
- She kind of does.

155
00:12:47,767 --> 00:12:48,935
Darn you.

156
00:12:49,936 --> 00:12:52,104
She's absolutely gorgeous.

157
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:54,691
Hey, student. Quiet.

158
00:12:55,900 --> 00:12:59,237
Who is your boyfriend into right now?

159
00:12:59,779 --> 00:13:02,490
- It's you.
- She's right! It's you!

160
00:13:05,576 --> 00:13:06,702
You guys are right!

161
00:13:06,703 --> 00:13:09,121
- Yes!
- Yes!

162
00:13:09,122 --> 00:13:10,790
- It's Nam Da-reum.
- She's right.

163
00:13:11,165 --> 00:13:12,624
Instructor and student.

164
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,794
It's me.

165
00:13:15,003 --> 00:13:18,255
Just an instructor and a student.

166
00:13:18,256 --> 00:13:20,425
Yes, it's me.

167
00:13:30,435 --> 00:13:31,601
What?

168
00:13:31,602 --> 00:13:33,313
I'm sorry. I'm late.

169
00:13:34,856 --> 00:13:36,858
How did you get here?

170
00:13:38,985 --> 00:13:40,862
I'll drink this
as punishment for being late.

171
00:13:41,321 --> 00:13:42,488
As you should.

172
00:13:43,031 --> 00:13:44,073
- Oh, wow.
- Oh, my.

173
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:46,159
All right.

174
00:13:48,119 --> 00:13:50,079
- That's cool.
- Lucky you.

175
00:13:54,709 --> 00:13:57,044
We're going for round two, right?

176
00:13:57,045 --> 00:13:58,338
What round two?

177
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,466
But we should.

178
00:14:03,468 --> 00:14:04,718
Please excuse us.

179
00:14:04,719 --> 00:14:07,471
I'll schedule something
more proper next time.

180
00:14:07,472 --> 00:14:09,057
Hey, man.

181
00:14:13,770 --> 00:14:14,896
Stop.

182
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:19,316
I'm watching you.

183
00:14:19,317 --> 00:14:23,613
- Stop.
- If you ever make my Da-reum cry

184
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:27,367
you will cry tears of blood, man.
Got it?

185
00:14:28,618 --> 00:14:29,786
Got it?

186
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:32,372
Right. Yes.

187
00:14:33,539 --> 00:14:35,875
We should go, Ms. Da-reum.

188
00:14:37,960 --> 00:14:40,128
- Bye, girls.
- Bye.

189
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,297
See you soon.

190
00:14:41,422 --> 00:14:44,049
- So, round two?
- What round two? Let's go home.

191
00:14:44,050 --> 00:14:46,052
Hey, do you want to go for round two?

192
00:14:47,095 --> 00:14:48,262
Mi-mi.

193
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:58,272
Mi-mi.

194
00:14:59,482 --> 00:15:01,067
I really thought

195
00:15:01,859 --> 00:15:03,653
we had something going on.

196
00:15:04,821 --> 00:15:05,905
Min-woo.

197
00:15:07,281 --> 00:15:08,658
Do you really like me?

198
00:15:09,075 --> 00:15:10,493
I fell for you at first sight.

199
00:15:10,952 --> 00:15:14,122
When I work, eat, shower

200
00:15:14,414 --> 00:15:17,917
or even sit in the restroom,
you're all I think about.

201
00:15:22,547 --> 00:15:24,424
The thought of you

202
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:27,468
never leaves my mind all day long.

203
00:15:33,349 --> 00:15:35,143
Do you remember

204
00:15:36,227 --> 00:15:37,311
my ideal type?

205
00:15:37,812 --> 00:15:38,980
Your ideal type?

206
00:15:39,814 --> 00:15:43,401
A competent guy who's a good kisser?

207
00:15:43,734 --> 00:15:45,194
I hate bad kissers.

208
00:16:31,908 --> 00:16:33,117
Did we kiss for real?

209
00:16:33,743 --> 00:16:35,995
This is insane!

210
00:16:36,496 --> 00:16:38,580
See you tomorrow, Mi-mi!

211
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:39,832
Yes!

212
00:16:49,091 --> 00:16:50,384
I'm fine now.

213
00:16:54,972 --> 00:16:57,058
Are you mad that I couldn't make it?

214
00:16:58,476 --> 00:16:59,477
No.

215
00:16:59,936 --> 00:17:02,522
I'm not that petty.

216
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:05,525
Then why are you pouting?

217
00:17:10,655 --> 00:17:13,699
I heard you were close
to Ms. Han Jeong-yeon

218
00:17:14,075 --> 00:17:15,201
back in high school.

219
00:17:15,868 --> 00:17:18,162
Oh, yes. Right.

220
00:17:19,664 --> 00:17:20,790
We were friends.

221
00:17:23,668 --> 00:17:24,752
Is that all?

222
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:29,006
That's all.

223
00:17:36,722 --> 00:17:38,391
Kim Min-woo, you punk.

224
00:17:39,684 --> 00:17:41,561
Ms. Da-reum.

225
00:17:42,103 --> 00:17:44,230
I heard Ms. Han was your first love.

226
00:17:45,398 --> 00:17:48,025
- Well, it's...
- Was it nice to reunite with her?

227
00:17:48,401 --> 00:17:49,860
That you even missed our dinner?

228
00:17:50,403 --> 00:17:51,571
Don't take it the wrong way.

229
00:17:52,238 --> 00:17:53,406
It's all in the past.

230
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:59,036
She proposed a project,
so the meeting took a while.

231
00:18:00,830 --> 00:18:01,956
What is it?

232
00:18:06,752 --> 00:18:08,421
It's very important for Appello.

233
00:18:09,171 --> 00:18:11,382
It's a bit sensitive,
so I can't disclose everything.

234
00:18:12,675 --> 00:18:14,260
But I wouldn't lie to you.

235
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:18,222
Can you give me a little more time?

236
00:18:23,060 --> 00:18:24,562
Don't ever get anxious.

237
00:18:31,819 --> 00:18:33,404
Because the one I like right now...

238
00:18:35,573 --> 00:18:36,616
is you, Ms. Da-reum.

239
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:42,663
I know that.

240
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:46,250
Trust me, okay?

241
00:19:07,605 --> 00:19:09,105
THE CAT I MET ON MY WALK
REMINDED ME OF YOU

242
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:10,441
IT WAS CHATTY AND CUTE

243
00:19:22,119 --> 00:19:23,579
HAN JEONG-YEON

244
00:19:24,872 --> 00:19:27,416
- Hey.
- I just met with Ha-gi.

245
00:19:28,334 --> 00:19:29,877
What were you two talking about?

246
00:19:30,419 --> 00:19:31,962
You know, old memories.

247
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:34,882
You told me to win his heart.

248
00:19:36,425 --> 00:19:37,426
And?

249
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:40,721
It killed my pride.

250
00:19:41,472 --> 00:19:44,266
He seemed unbothered
by his first love.

251
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:46,811
I might start trying harder.

252
00:19:49,605 --> 00:19:50,940
What do you mean?

253
00:19:51,440 --> 00:19:54,068
What's wrong?
Wasn't this what you wanted?

254
00:19:55,736 --> 00:19:57,363
You don't have to feel so guilty.

255
00:19:58,698 --> 00:19:59,699
Because

256
00:20:00,825 --> 00:20:01,992
I want Ha-gi back

257
00:20:03,327 --> 00:20:04,912
for myself again.

258
00:20:20,511 --> 00:20:21,971
IF YOU DON'T KNOW HAN,
YOU DON'T KNOW FASHION

259
00:20:28,185 --> 00:20:30,688
CLOTHES THAT STAY WITH YOU

260
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:35,192
"Clothes that stay with you."

261
00:21:01,469 --> 00:21:03,261
You want to work
with a designated employee?

262
00:21:03,262 --> 00:21:06,390
Yes, it's weird to reach out
to the CEO every single time.

263
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:10,895
Did you say it was Ms. Nam Da-reum
who wrote the proposal?

264
00:21:13,522 --> 00:21:14,523
I want her.

265
00:21:21,238 --> 00:21:23,991
- Why Ms. Da-reum of all people?
- I told you already.

266
00:21:24,325 --> 00:21:26,327
I liked Appello's proposal.

267
00:21:26,911 --> 00:21:29,997
I loved the level of understanding
she has of my brand.

268
00:21:31,999 --> 00:21:35,210
I'll see if Ms. Da-reum
will be interested.

269
00:21:35,211 --> 00:21:36,253
I can ask now.

270
00:21:46,263 --> 00:21:47,348
Ms. Nam Da-reum?

271
00:21:51,143 --> 00:21:53,312
- Yes.
- I loved your proposal.

272
00:21:54,271 --> 00:21:56,816
I need someone who'll handle
my business with Appello.

273
00:21:57,066 --> 00:21:59,860
Would you like to lead the project?

274
00:22:05,449 --> 00:22:08,244
I'd be happy to,
if Mr. Kang is okay with it.

275
00:22:09,954 --> 00:22:11,372
It's a great opportunity, I guess.

276
00:22:12,665 --> 00:22:14,166
But it's your opinion that matters.

277
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:17,878
What do you think?

278
00:22:21,382 --> 00:22:22,508
In that case

279
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:25,803
I want to do it.

280
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:30,683
Excellent. I look forward to it.

281
00:22:50,202 --> 00:22:51,829
You don't have to feel so guilty.

282
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:54,498
Because

283
00:22:55,583 --> 00:22:59,587
I want Ha-gi back for myself again.

284
00:23:08,554 --> 00:23:09,555
WON-BIN

285
00:23:11,181 --> 00:23:12,265
Hey, Won-bin.

286
00:23:12,266 --> 00:23:14,143
I've got bad news, Chan.

287
00:23:19,273 --> 00:23:20,316
You're here.

288
00:23:21,025 --> 00:23:22,026
Let's go.

289
00:23:24,778 --> 00:23:26,238
First, put these on.

290
00:23:26,572 --> 00:23:28,157
No, I didn't do anything wrong.

291
00:23:29,116 --> 00:23:32,369
You didn't leave behind
weird photos or videos, right?

292
00:23:32,828 --> 00:23:34,455
What do you take me for?

293
00:23:35,915 --> 00:23:39,375
Anyway, Jinu and Teo
were the ones who got hacked.

294
00:23:39,376 --> 00:23:42,462
Why are you getting summoned? Gosh.

295
00:23:42,463 --> 00:23:43,881
I'm nervous to death.

296
00:23:44,798 --> 00:23:45,965
There it is.

297
00:23:45,966 --> 00:23:50,220
INVESTIGATION DIVISION

298
00:23:50,512 --> 00:23:53,474
Thankfully, the hacker was arrested
before any information got leaked.

299
00:23:54,308 --> 00:23:56,726
The data he used to blackmail them

300
00:23:56,727 --> 00:24:01,439
included unreleased songs and videos
related to you, Mr. Lee.

301
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:02,608
I wanted to check with you.

302
00:24:06,403 --> 00:24:07,654
Wait.

303
00:24:07,655 --> 00:24:10,282
These are materials you used
for your album preparations.

304
00:24:10,741 --> 00:24:12,117
It was supposedly
for the five of you.

305
00:24:13,994 --> 00:24:15,787
It must've been important.

306
00:24:15,788 --> 00:24:19,625
They even gave the hacker money
and tried to stop it.

307
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:25,089
They tried that hard?

308
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:28,592
And they didn't even tell me.

309
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:41,647
Boys.

310
00:24:45,776 --> 00:24:46,819
Chan.

311
00:25:00,749 --> 00:25:03,168
You should've called me first
when this happened.

312
00:25:03,627 --> 00:25:07,089
What money did you have
to hand over to that guy?

313
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:09,425
I mean, it included Chan's data...

314
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:13,177
and songs you worked on for years.

315
00:25:13,178 --> 00:25:14,637
We disbanded a decade ago.

316
00:25:14,638 --> 00:25:16,056
Why are you still like this?

317
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:18,558
Go live your life now. Please.

318
00:25:18,559 --> 00:25:20,519
You may be done, but not us.

319
00:25:22,021 --> 00:25:23,063
For us

320
00:25:23,897 --> 00:25:25,190
D.N.X is everything.

321
00:25:28,819 --> 00:25:29,820
Sorry.

322
00:25:30,571 --> 00:25:32,865
We'll try not to stand in your way
from now on.

323
00:25:35,034 --> 00:25:36,285
Hey, Jinu.

324
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:37,911
Jinu.

325
00:25:55,846 --> 00:25:57,848
You must be working hard
for the presentation

326
00:25:58,182 --> 00:26:00,976
so I prepared this meeting
to show you my support.

327
00:26:01,268 --> 00:26:03,145
There's nothing much for us to do.

328
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:06,065
We've caught up with Appello
as soon as our platform launched.

329
00:26:06,607 --> 00:26:08,275
We'll take first place in no time.

330
00:26:09,735 --> 00:26:13,280
And we're almost done
with customer profiling.

331
00:26:14,573 --> 00:26:18,911
HAN's customers must be those
who are drawn to scarcity.

332
00:26:27,461 --> 00:26:31,131
HAN's customers must be those
who are drawn to scarcity.

333
00:26:32,466 --> 00:26:35,469
The desire to have something
that you cannot have.

334
00:26:35,928 --> 00:26:38,931
You're right. People line up
before the opening because of that.

335
00:26:39,598 --> 00:26:40,724
Scarcity.

336
00:26:42,726 --> 00:26:43,852
Scarcity.

337
00:26:53,946 --> 00:26:55,114
Scarcity.

338
00:26:55,823 --> 00:26:57,491
We should approach the Korean market

339
00:26:57,950 --> 00:26:59,618
with the same
limited-edition strategy.

340
00:27:00,869 --> 00:27:02,371
That's an interesting take.

341
00:27:03,413 --> 00:27:04,665
What does

342
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:07,292
Appello think?

343
00:27:11,797 --> 00:27:12,881
I can't say for sure.

344
00:27:14,341 --> 00:27:15,384
We're still

345
00:27:16,552 --> 00:27:17,594
working on it.

346
00:27:23,642 --> 00:27:25,853
Goodness. We should eat.

347
00:27:28,063 --> 00:27:29,982
It looks great.

348
00:27:48,876 --> 00:27:52,129
Something's going on between
Kang Ha-gi and Han Jeong-yeon.

349
00:27:52,462 --> 00:27:53,505
Find out what it is.

350
00:28:01,388 --> 00:28:03,640
HERITY FACTORY:
MODERN POP-UP SHOWROOM

351
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:09,771
You're still here.

352
00:28:11,064 --> 00:28:12,858
Hey, Director Lee.

353
00:28:18,697 --> 00:28:20,782
I was passing by,
and I saw the lights on.

354
00:28:21,241 --> 00:28:23,368
If anyone is working until now,
it had to be you.

355
00:28:24,745 --> 00:28:26,622
I had to work on something.

356
00:28:27,831 --> 00:28:29,208
Don't you go on dates?

357
00:28:34,546 --> 00:28:35,714
I know, right?

358
00:28:42,179 --> 00:28:44,389
Have you eaten?

359
00:28:49,645 --> 00:28:50,771
I met

360
00:28:52,356 --> 00:28:54,733
Jinu and Teo at the police station.

361
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:56,610
The police station?

362
00:28:57,903 --> 00:29:00,030
They got hacked

363
00:29:00,864 --> 00:29:03,283
and the data
was all about D.N.X's comeback.

364
00:29:06,203 --> 00:29:07,829
They still haven't given up
on that dream.

365
00:29:10,290 --> 00:29:11,917
I didn't know they were so desperate.

366
00:29:16,505 --> 00:29:18,048
But you feel the same way.

367
00:29:20,425 --> 00:29:23,887
Wasn't that why you had been
working on that fan song?

368
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:31,979
You're right.

369
00:29:36,233 --> 00:29:37,776
But I guess I must have no courage.

370
00:29:38,568 --> 00:29:42,364
The courage to throw away
great opportunities

371
00:29:43,532 --> 00:29:44,992
and my career.

372
00:29:47,536 --> 00:29:50,998
Is it because
that's the practical choice?

373
00:30:01,216 --> 00:30:03,176
I should focus on my movie, right?

374
00:30:09,683 --> 00:30:10,767
Whatever choice you make

375
00:30:12,311 --> 00:30:14,563
I want you to do

376
00:30:15,689 --> 00:30:16,857
what your heart tells you to do.

377
00:30:18,775 --> 00:30:20,485
Something for yourself.

378
00:30:37,711 --> 00:30:39,004
Whatever choice you make

379
00:30:39,504 --> 00:30:43,216
I want you to do
what your heart tells you to do.

380
00:30:44,051 --> 00:30:45,719
Something for yourself.

381
00:31:16,666 --> 00:31:19,169
- All right!
- Come with me.

382
00:31:21,088 --> 00:31:22,714
I'm over here.

383
00:31:28,970 --> 00:31:29,971
Ms. Da-reum.

384
00:31:30,514 --> 00:31:31,515
Look.

385
00:31:40,982 --> 00:31:42,150
What is this?

386
00:31:43,151 --> 00:31:45,821
It's so pretty. What is this?

387
00:31:46,363 --> 00:31:48,657
My gosh. Did you prepare all this?

388
00:31:53,537 --> 00:31:55,496
How pretty.

389
00:31:55,497 --> 00:31:57,499
When did you look these up
and prepare everything?

390
00:31:58,834 --> 00:32:00,043
Well, you know.

391
00:32:00,752 --> 00:32:01,962
I just saw it by coincidence.

392
00:32:03,630 --> 00:32:04,714
Is that true?

393
00:32:08,343 --> 00:32:09,511
Try this.

394
00:32:15,684 --> 00:32:17,269
- Do you like it?
- This is good too.

395
00:32:32,993 --> 00:32:36,246
The weekend feels so short.

396
00:32:38,623 --> 00:32:40,041
I don't want to go to work tomorrow.

397
00:32:44,880 --> 00:32:46,506
How can you say that
in front of your CEO?

398
00:32:47,340 --> 00:32:48,341
What?

399
00:32:50,510 --> 00:32:51,845
I was talking to my boyfriend.

400
00:33:18,038 --> 00:33:19,289
4 P.M. GO TO THE LAKE
5 P.M. WATCH THE REFLECTION

401
00:33:24,503 --> 00:33:27,046
Do you want to move to the lake?

402
00:33:27,047 --> 00:33:28,965
- Why?
- Because...

403
00:33:29,799 --> 00:33:31,259
I heard it's beautiful at sunset.

404
00:33:31,801 --> 00:33:32,969
To show me the light reflection?

405
00:33:36,056 --> 00:33:38,892
But I just want to stay here.

406
00:33:54,866 --> 00:33:56,450
1 P.M. LUNCH AT THE RESTAURANT
2 P.M. CAFE

407
00:33:56,451 --> 00:33:58,119
3 P.M. PICNIC ON THE GRASS
4 P.M. GO TO THE LAKE

408
00:34:01,039 --> 00:34:02,999
We don't have to move
according to your plan.

409
00:34:06,169 --> 00:34:08,713
Why are you trying so hard
to impress me today?

410
00:34:11,299 --> 00:34:15,011
I didn't get to meet
your friends properly last time.

411
00:34:16,805 --> 00:34:18,097
And we haven't seen
each other lately.

412
00:34:18,098 --> 00:34:19,266
Did that bother you?

413
00:34:22,978 --> 00:34:25,981
I wanted to do it right this time.

414
00:34:28,191 --> 00:34:31,778
It's because of Ms. Han, isn't it?

415
00:34:37,242 --> 00:34:39,578
- I...
- You said I had nothing to worry.

416
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:45,292
I decided to take on HAN
because I trust you.

417
00:34:46,251 --> 00:34:48,210
You don't have to try that hard.

418
00:34:48,211 --> 00:34:49,921
I just like it when we're together.

419
00:35:01,224 --> 00:35:02,350
Thank you.

420
00:35:06,771 --> 00:35:07,814
Do you want to lie down again?

421
00:35:08,648 --> 00:35:10,525
No, I want to stay like this.

422
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:20,535
Beyond the forgotten memories

423
00:35:21,202 --> 00:35:23,246
I want to go up into the sky

424
00:35:24,164 --> 00:35:25,290
Get on

425
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:28,668
Oh, gosh.

426
00:35:31,546 --> 00:35:33,340
It's been so long
that I don't remember anything.

427
00:35:34,424 --> 00:35:36,551
You're getting old.

428
00:35:36,801 --> 00:35:38,344
Wait till you're my age.

429
00:35:38,345 --> 00:35:40,347
It's not easy to dance like this.

430
00:35:40,513 --> 00:35:43,891
Anyway, it's so nice
to practice together.

431
00:35:43,892 --> 00:35:47,020
- Me too.
- You're grossing me out. Get off me.

432
00:35:48,313 --> 00:35:49,981
It would've been nice
if Chan was here.

433
00:35:58,156 --> 00:36:00,241
Don't get your hopes up.

434
00:36:01,368 --> 00:36:03,703
D.N.X means nothing
to a top star like him.

435
00:36:04,704 --> 00:36:06,247
He's on his way to Hollywood.

436
00:36:08,917 --> 00:36:10,293
Why don't we try it again?

437
00:36:11,169 --> 00:36:12,504
Let's start from "Get on."

438
00:36:26,142 --> 00:36:28,937
MYEONGMYEONG BUILDING

439
00:36:32,065 --> 00:36:37,153
MYU DANCE STUDIO

440
00:37:08,351 --> 00:37:09,394
Roy.

441
00:37:11,938 --> 00:37:14,149
I don't care who you like.

442
00:37:15,859 --> 00:37:16,860
But

443
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:20,113
it's too much for us
to handle right now.

444
00:37:22,782 --> 00:37:23,783
Let's keep it a secret.

445
00:37:25,577 --> 00:37:26,661
Later...

446
00:37:28,288 --> 00:37:29,873
When things get better...

447
00:37:32,041 --> 00:37:33,168
Just until then.

448
00:37:38,798 --> 00:37:39,841
Okay.

449
00:37:49,809 --> 00:37:52,353
SHOCKING PICTURES OF ROY
AND HIS BOYFRIEND

450
00:37:56,441 --> 00:37:58,860
DARK CLOUDS OVER D.N.X,
ALL EYES ON THEIR FUTURE

451
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:00,320
Stop reading it.

452
00:38:01,780 --> 00:38:04,449
- Chan, what do we do now?
- That's why I told you...

453
00:38:06,826 --> 00:38:08,745
You should've been more careful, Roy.

454
00:38:14,417 --> 00:38:15,751
Roy!

455
00:38:15,752 --> 00:38:17,669
- Hey.
- Don't do this to Roy.

456
00:38:17,670 --> 00:38:19,630
- Stop.
- Move. Get out of my way!

457
00:38:19,631 --> 00:38:21,549
- Don't do this too.
- I said, move!

458
00:38:23,343 --> 00:38:24,761
You're no different.

459
00:38:25,053 --> 00:38:27,472
The two of you ruined
everything we built!

460
00:38:49,160 --> 00:38:51,078
QUICK DELIVERY

461
00:38:51,079 --> 00:38:53,665
- Hi, I'm back.
- Good job today.

462
00:38:54,707 --> 00:38:57,960
Hey, the boss saw him.
He really is a celebrity.

463
00:38:57,961 --> 00:39:01,338
He was a member of some group
called D.N. something.

464
00:39:01,339 --> 00:39:05,260
- Don't be ridiculous.
- But it's true. I swear.

465
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:06,885
- Want to bet 50,000 won?
- You called it.

466
00:39:06,886 --> 00:39:08,262
- Yes.
- Deal.

467
00:39:08,263 --> 00:39:10,390
You said 50,000 won.

468
00:39:16,437 --> 00:39:19,481
Hey, take off your helmet
for a second.

469
00:39:19,482 --> 00:39:22,401
We've worked together for months,
but I still haven't seen your face.

470
00:39:22,402 --> 00:39:23,986
Hey, I heard you were an idol.

471
00:39:23,987 --> 00:39:26,113
- Is it true? Show me.
- No.

472
00:39:26,114 --> 00:39:28,156
- Hey, take it off.
- Take it off, will you?

473
00:39:28,157 --> 00:39:30,869
- Why won't you take it off?
- Let me see your face.

474
00:39:33,496 --> 00:39:36,499
Seriously, don't you have
anything else to do?

475
00:39:38,710 --> 00:39:41,461
What on earth are you doing
when you should be

476
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:42,963
working hard at this busy hour?

477
00:39:42,964 --> 00:39:44,007
Who are you?

478
00:39:48,511 --> 00:39:49,762
Triple the delivery fee.

479
00:39:50,513 --> 00:39:51,973
There's a limited time event.

480
00:39:52,599 --> 00:39:53,892
TRIPLE THE DELIVERY FEE
TIME EVENT

481
00:39:55,101 --> 00:39:57,185
- It's true.
- I can't miss this.

482
00:39:57,186 --> 00:39:58,646
I'll see you when I come back.

483
00:39:58,897 --> 00:40:01,232
It's only on for two hours.

484
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:06,112
Stop bothering him.

485
00:40:07,530 --> 00:40:08,531
Thank you.

486
00:40:11,659 --> 00:40:13,328
Then can you make some time for me?

487
00:40:26,883 --> 00:40:28,092
Thank you, Seul-a.

488
00:40:29,385 --> 00:40:31,512
That's all you drink.

489
00:40:33,181 --> 00:40:34,515
How did you know?

490
00:40:35,350 --> 00:40:36,643
Because I was your fan.

491
00:40:38,436 --> 00:40:40,104
No, it's not that I was.

492
00:40:40,605 --> 00:40:42,065
I still am.

493
00:40:45,944 --> 00:40:49,948
I started
this delivery job to find you.

494
00:40:51,282 --> 00:40:54,035
- What?
- To see if it really was you.

495
00:40:54,452 --> 00:40:55,495
Then I realized it was you.

496
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:04,629
Honestly, I don't care what you do.

497
00:41:05,755 --> 00:41:07,548
But you never take the helmet off.

498
00:41:10,259 --> 00:41:11,970
That really upsets me.

499
00:41:13,638 --> 00:41:17,266
I know that you feel bad
about what happened to the team.

500
00:41:20,436 --> 00:41:21,896
But I don't want you

501
00:41:23,272 --> 00:41:26,401
to live as if you never existed
just because of that.

502
00:41:28,194 --> 00:41:30,613
I've never been ashamed of you.

503
00:41:30,947 --> 00:41:32,782
Back then or now.

504
00:41:33,950 --> 00:41:34,993
So...

505
00:41:36,911 --> 00:41:39,497
don't hide yourself,
at least from me.

506
00:42:35,219 --> 00:42:38,806
I made a list of pop-up stores
that would fit HAN's concept.

507
00:42:41,392 --> 00:42:43,310
I like the space.

508
00:42:43,311 --> 00:42:44,644
The location is good.

509
00:42:44,645 --> 00:42:47,856
Only global luxury brands have held
pop-up stores there.

510
00:42:47,857 --> 00:42:49,817
There's intense competition
for the space, not just from us.

511
00:42:50,193 --> 00:42:51,611
It must've required a lot of legwork.

512
00:42:52,445 --> 00:42:53,446
Not at all.

513
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:56,365
However

514
00:42:57,825 --> 00:42:59,410
the streets may be crowded

515
00:42:59,911 --> 00:43:01,662
but none of them are my customers.

516
00:43:02,914 --> 00:43:03,915
I beg your pardon?

517
00:43:05,333 --> 00:43:08,002
Is this all you prepared?

518
00:43:17,929 --> 00:43:19,222
PROJECT PROPOSAL

519
00:43:22,517 --> 00:43:23,726
Wait.

520
00:43:26,187 --> 00:43:29,315
Actually, aside from the places
you saw in the meeting

521
00:43:29,857 --> 00:43:32,068
I have another one in mind.

522
00:43:43,454 --> 00:43:44,539
Where are we?

523
00:43:46,165 --> 00:43:47,250
This is Ikseon-dong.

524
00:43:49,585 --> 00:43:51,170
I looked into why HAN's main branch
in Paris is

525
00:43:51,629 --> 00:43:55,257
located in the old streets
of Saint-Germain

526
00:43:55,258 --> 00:43:58,594
instead of Rue Saint-Honoré,
where all the luxury brands are.

527
00:43:59,595 --> 00:44:02,557
It's a place with unique cafes,
private bookstores

528
00:44:02,974 --> 00:44:04,308
and a lot of vintage shops.

529
00:44:04,809 --> 00:44:07,770
It's where people
with a strong sense of style go.

530
00:44:08,563 --> 00:44:11,274
I thought about where those people
would go in Korea.

531
00:44:12,483 --> 00:44:13,484
And?

532
00:44:13,901 --> 00:44:16,028
My impression is that HAN's customers

533
00:44:16,696 --> 00:44:19,907
like to walk, explore, and stay.

534
00:44:21,367 --> 00:44:25,246
They buy something
that reflects what they like.

535
00:44:27,582 --> 00:44:30,793
I'm finally starting to like it.

536
00:44:33,880 --> 00:44:34,881
Sure.

537
00:44:35,339 --> 00:44:37,300
Let's keep looking around.

538
00:44:40,469 --> 00:44:41,679
Yes, Ms. Han.

539
00:44:47,393 --> 00:44:49,520
My first brand didn't work out.

540
00:44:50,730 --> 00:44:52,773
Then is HAN your second one?

541
00:44:54,692 --> 00:44:56,986
I started it with a friend
from fashion school

542
00:44:57,528 --> 00:44:59,030
and we got good responses
when we first opened.

543
00:45:00,489 --> 00:45:01,574
Then why didn't it work out?

544
00:45:03,117 --> 00:45:05,493
My friend went behind my back

545
00:45:05,494 --> 00:45:07,163
and I lost everything
to a major corporation.

546
00:45:08,080 --> 00:45:09,916
I started from scratch again.

547
00:45:10,541 --> 00:45:11,834
That led to HAN now.

548
00:45:15,671 --> 00:45:17,006
It must've been tough.

549
00:45:17,757 --> 00:45:20,551
It was, but that helped me grow up.

550
00:45:21,427 --> 00:45:25,181
It taught me what I was capable of.

551
00:45:25,932 --> 00:45:28,476
I realized I was relying
on her sense a lot

552
00:45:28,768 --> 00:45:30,102
and not my own.

553
00:45:31,729 --> 00:45:35,024
So when I started HAN,
I focused on myself

554
00:45:35,858 --> 00:45:39,779
like what I could present
and what I was good at.

555
00:45:42,323 --> 00:45:44,825
She's undeniably cool.

556
00:45:47,745 --> 00:45:49,121
What about you, Ms. Da-reum?

557
00:45:49,789 --> 00:45:53,417
Do you feel like the work you do
at Appello is truly yours?

558
00:45:57,755 --> 00:46:02,134
I'm still learning.
I think I'm getting there.

559
00:46:06,555 --> 00:46:07,640
By any chance

560
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:11,519
does my relationship
with Mr. Kang bother you?

561
00:46:20,653 --> 00:46:24,115
I'd be lying if I said no.

562
00:46:25,533 --> 00:46:27,033
That's very honest.

563
00:46:27,034 --> 00:46:28,077
But I...

564
00:46:28,911 --> 00:46:30,746
I trust the person I'm dating.

565
00:46:35,876 --> 00:46:36,919
Do you?

566
00:46:48,264 --> 00:46:49,973
In the end

567
00:46:49,974 --> 00:46:52,727
HAN's customers must be those
who are drawn to scarcity.

568
00:46:56,689 --> 00:46:57,982
Come on.

569
00:46:59,025 --> 00:47:00,568
What are you so worried about?

570
00:47:08,492 --> 00:47:11,453
Ms. Han Jeong-yeon seems kind to us.

571
00:47:11,454 --> 00:47:12,621
You shouldn't worry so much.

572
00:47:16,625 --> 00:47:17,752
Seong-wook.

573
00:47:18,586 --> 00:47:21,756
SE's ideas are too similar to ours.

574
00:47:24,967 --> 00:47:29,221
But it's normal for ideas like that
to overlap in this field.

575
00:47:30,056 --> 00:47:32,266
Hey, don't you think
you're being too sensitive lately?

576
00:47:35,603 --> 00:47:37,229
I wish that was the case.

577
00:47:39,482 --> 00:47:41,025
Don't worry.

578
00:47:47,823 --> 00:47:50,284
Come on.
There's nothing to worry about.

579
00:47:51,285 --> 00:47:52,328
Okay?

580
00:47:52,995 --> 00:47:53,996
Right.

581
00:47:56,624 --> 00:47:58,834
Thank you for everything today.
I appreciate it.

582
00:48:00,252 --> 00:48:02,421
Is there anything else
I can help you with?

583
00:48:03,422 --> 00:48:05,299
It's okay. I'm expecting someone.

584
00:48:06,467 --> 00:48:10,596
- Bye now.
- Okay, I'll see you later.

585
00:48:33,619 --> 00:48:37,623
I'm going to tell him
I pulled it off today.

586
00:48:45,131 --> 00:48:48,049
The person you're trying to reach
is not available.

587
00:48:48,050 --> 00:48:50,344
Please leave a message
after the beep.

588
00:49:31,302 --> 00:49:32,886
ANNUAL PERFORMANCE REPORT

589
00:49:32,887 --> 00:49:35,306
SE CORPORATION QUARTERLY PERFORMANCE
BY DIVISION

590
00:49:38,684 --> 00:49:40,351
ILLEGAL SUBCONTRACT
INVESTIGATION REPORT

591
00:49:40,352 --> 00:49:42,187
SE CORPORATION BUSINESS ANALYSIS

592
00:49:42,188 --> 00:49:43,981
CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION LEAK

593
00:49:53,032 --> 00:49:56,994
SE spent too much on marketing
after starting their platform.

594
00:49:58,662 --> 00:49:59,830
It's like they were gambling.

595
00:50:00,581 --> 00:50:01,665
How did you secure this?

596
00:50:02,166 --> 00:50:04,126
Through the agency
that consulted SE:ON.

597
00:50:04,418 --> 00:50:07,713
I've been tracking their movement
since before I came to Korea.

598
00:50:10,132 --> 00:50:11,926
It's always the same for SE.

599
00:50:12,760 --> 00:50:15,679
They call it
collaboration and investment

600
00:50:16,680 --> 00:50:18,724
but all they're thinking about
is taking over other companies.

601
00:50:22,645 --> 00:50:23,896
I know it from experience.

602
00:50:27,274 --> 00:50:29,026
They approached us the same way.

603
00:50:38,035 --> 00:50:39,745
MS. NAM DA-REUM:
WHERE ARE YOU?

604
00:50:40,120 --> 00:50:41,872
I JUST FINISHED

605
00:50:59,515 --> 00:51:01,433
WHERE ARE YOU?
I JUST FINISHED

606
00:51:09,608 --> 00:51:12,152
CEO KANG HA-GI OF APPELLO

607
00:51:19,326 --> 00:51:21,078
I can't even call him.

608
00:51:26,584 --> 00:51:27,793
I'm so pathetic.

609
00:51:32,047 --> 00:51:33,716
CHAN

610
00:51:40,931 --> 00:51:42,808
- Hi, Chan.
- What are you up to, Da-reum?

611
00:51:44,810 --> 00:51:46,812
Nothing much.

612
00:51:47,438 --> 00:51:48,772
Then do you want to listen to this?

613
00:51:50,941 --> 00:51:52,026
Listen to what?

614
00:51:53,569 --> 00:51:54,653
One second.

615
00:52:43,243 --> 00:52:44,244
What do you think?

616
00:52:46,580 --> 00:52:48,540
I love it.

617
00:52:50,125 --> 00:52:54,380
It feels comforting.

618
00:52:57,424 --> 00:52:59,802
I've been stuck,
but you helped me work through it.

619
00:53:00,844 --> 00:53:02,011
I did?

620
00:53:02,012 --> 00:53:05,099
I just went with my heart
like you said.

621
00:53:07,017 --> 00:53:10,437
Go with my heart...

622
00:53:12,981 --> 00:53:14,483
I should've done this earlier.

623
00:53:15,609 --> 00:53:16,777
Thanks, Da-reum.

624
00:53:21,073 --> 00:53:22,658
I said that...

625
00:53:24,702 --> 00:53:26,328
when I couldn't even do it myself.

626
00:53:27,204 --> 00:53:28,414
What's that?

627
00:53:30,207 --> 00:53:31,541
Nothing.

628
00:53:31,542 --> 00:53:34,086
Let me hear it when you're done.

629
00:53:34,503 --> 00:53:36,171
I'm sorry. I have to go.

630
00:54:10,581 --> 00:54:11,957
Want a glass?

631
00:54:14,877 --> 00:54:15,878
No, thanks.

632
00:54:19,339 --> 00:54:20,966
When can I talk to you again

633
00:54:21,675 --> 00:54:23,218
not as the CEO of Appello

634
00:54:24,052 --> 00:54:25,763
but as Kang Ha-gi?

635
00:54:27,431 --> 00:54:28,515
Next time.

636
00:54:29,099 --> 00:54:30,100
With Chan too.

637
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:45,324
MISSED CALL
MS. NAM DA-REUM

638
00:55:04,384 --> 00:55:05,469
By any chance

639
00:55:06,512 --> 00:55:08,931
does my relationship
with Mr. Kang bother you?

640
00:55:11,350 --> 00:55:12,518
But I...

641
00:55:13,602 --> 00:55:15,521
I trust the person I'm dating.

642
00:55:18,482 --> 00:55:19,525
Do you?

643
00:55:20,484 --> 00:55:22,277
It's okay. I'm expecting someone.

644
00:56:05,153 --> 00:56:06,321
Is it too late?

645
00:56:08,115 --> 00:56:09,324
I missed you.

646
00:56:18,292 --> 00:56:19,293
What's wrong?

647
00:56:20,627 --> 00:56:21,712
Is something the matter?

648
00:56:24,548 --> 00:56:25,549
Yes.

649
00:56:26,967 --> 00:56:28,010
I saw you

650
00:56:28,802 --> 00:56:31,263
entering Ms. Han's hotel earlier.

651
00:56:35,517 --> 00:56:38,604
Were you with her all this while?

652
00:56:44,192 --> 00:56:46,320
- I...
- You didn't tell me.

653
00:56:46,987 --> 00:56:48,447
And I couldn't reach you.

654
00:56:50,449 --> 00:56:53,118
If I hadn't seen you, I wouldn't have
known you were together.

655
00:56:53,452 --> 00:56:55,495
- It's a misunderstanding.
- If it's not, what is it?

656
00:57:03,378 --> 00:57:04,421
Later.

657
00:57:05,380 --> 00:57:06,590
I'll tell you later.

658
00:57:12,638 --> 00:57:13,680
I'm sorry.

659
00:57:20,062 --> 00:57:21,146
But I'm...

660
00:57:23,190 --> 00:57:26,360
I'm your girlfriend.

661
00:57:28,779 --> 00:57:31,198
How am I different from a stranger?

662
00:57:34,743 --> 00:57:35,744
Ms. Da-reum...

663
00:57:40,999 --> 00:57:42,042
I'm sorry.

664
00:57:43,919 --> 00:57:45,963
I can't pretend to be okay right now.

665
00:58:53,822 --> 00:58:56,032
- It's the final presentation data.
- Okay.

666
00:58:56,033 --> 00:58:57,451
CUSTOMER PROFILING REPORT
APPELLO

667
00:59:07,210 --> 00:59:08,378
But Mr. Kang

668
00:59:09,046 --> 00:59:12,006
this is completely different from
what we discussed in the meeting.

669
00:59:12,007 --> 00:59:13,008
Why did it change?

670
00:59:13,550 --> 00:59:14,926
I leaked that on purpose.

671
00:59:16,053 --> 00:59:17,220
This is the real data.

672
00:59:19,931 --> 00:59:21,558
We have to be careful
until the presentation.

673
00:59:25,062 --> 00:59:26,271
Please go over it.

674
00:59:27,981 --> 00:59:29,232
Yes, sir.

675
00:59:54,132 --> 00:59:55,217
Hello.

676
01:00:25,497 --> 01:00:27,331
They must've had a fight, right?

677
01:00:27,332 --> 01:00:28,958
Isn't this the first time
since they started dating?

678
01:00:28,959 --> 01:00:31,044
It's so obvious. It's suffocating me.

679
01:00:32,546 --> 01:00:34,798
I can feel it.

680
01:00:35,173 --> 01:00:36,174
What now?

681
01:00:36,842 --> 01:00:39,177
Maybe they're faking it,
so they won't get caught.

682
01:00:41,680 --> 01:00:42,806
What?

683
01:00:43,765 --> 01:00:44,891
But it's true.

684
01:00:45,475 --> 01:00:47,394
I'm very sharp, you know?

685
01:00:54,192 --> 01:00:55,235
Da-reum.

686
01:00:57,320 --> 01:01:00,781
- There you are.
- Are you here to see me?

687
01:01:00,782 --> 01:01:03,034
Yes, you said you wanted to hear
the fan song when it was ready.

688
01:01:03,785 --> 01:01:04,786
Oh, right.

689
01:01:08,373 --> 01:01:11,041
You didn't sound well last time
I talked to you on the phone.

690
01:01:11,042 --> 01:01:12,711
I was also worried if you were okay.

691
01:01:14,880 --> 01:01:17,257
I'm fine.
There's nothing to worry about.

692
01:01:18,925 --> 01:01:20,969
Should we listen to it
in the showroom? There are speakers.

693
01:01:21,469 --> 01:01:22,512
Sure.

694
01:01:27,893 --> 01:01:29,728
- Can you put it on bluetooth?
- Yes.

695
01:01:30,270 --> 01:01:31,771
SETTINGS

696
01:01:32,147 --> 01:01:36,276
I don't think she's caught on
to what we've been up to yet.

697
01:01:36,735 --> 01:01:38,570
I'm going to tell her the truth.

698
01:03:12,539 --> 01:03:16,293
MY BIAS, MY BOSS

699
01:03:26,886 --> 01:03:29,638
- It's the same, down to every word.
- This is crazy.

700
01:03:29,639 --> 01:03:31,391
How can it be the same?

701
01:03:31,975 --> 01:03:34,518
Mr. Kang didn't come to work today.

702
01:03:34,519 --> 01:03:36,186
He never once missed work

703
01:03:36,187 --> 01:03:37,522
rain or shine,
or even when he was sick.

704
01:03:38,690 --> 01:03:40,608
I'll stay by your side to the end.

705
01:03:42,319 --> 01:03:43,820
There's something I want to do.

706
01:03:44,195 --> 01:03:45,613
We never waited for you.

707
01:03:46,906 --> 01:03:49,283
I didn't want to hide it anymore.

708
01:03:49,284 --> 01:03:50,367
I LOVE LEE CHAN

709
01:03:50,368 --> 01:03:51,703
I wanted to show you

710
01:03:52,454 --> 01:03:55,123
that this is who I am,
and the part of me that loves you

711
01:03:56,291 --> 01:03:57,625
is also a part of who I am.
